00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:26.000
It was like, no, I don't want to do a series on

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:29.000
What's known as eschatology, like the end of all things

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.000
And it just gets so weird in Christian circles

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:38.000
And as we'll touch on, I think apocalyptic literature

00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:40.000
And stuff gets really misunderstood in the Bible

00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:44.000
And so it just, you know, end times kind of stuff

00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:45.000
Just like, ah

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:49.000
But what I've tried to kind of frame this up as

00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:52.000
Is to find what I feel are the most kind of

00:36:52.000 --> 00:36:55.000
Not only just biblically kind of faithful to the text

00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:58.000
But also just the most beautiful vision

00:36:58.000 --> 00:37:00.000
I can give us of the end

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:01.000
By the end, I don't just mean

00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:03.000
Like literally, the world's going to burn

00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:05.000
I mean the purpose, the telos

00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:09.000
The end to which God is calling us and all things

00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:14.000
And I really do believe it's an incredibly hopeful vision

00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:15.000
So if you've been here for these weeks

00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:17.000
You know we've been talking about the apocatastasis

00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:19.000
The big old fancy Greek word

00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:22.000
That just means the restoration of all things

00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:24.000
And that's the hopeful vision

00:37:24.000 --> 00:37:27.000
Is really that us and all creation will

00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:28.000
Right now as Romans 8 says

00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:31.000
We're groaning, all creation's groaning

00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:32.000
And we look around the world

00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:34.000
And we see that pain

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:38.000
And yet it's a kind of birth pain

00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:41.000
That actually God's up to something

00:37:41.000 --> 00:37:46.000
And there's a beautiful, healing, restorative end

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:47.000
For all of us

00:37:47.000 --> 00:37:49.000
So that's what I've been kind of pressing into

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:50.000
Even though it's been a little bit

00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:51.000
I know touch and go at times

00:37:51.000 --> 00:37:53.000
Because part of that is we have to touch on the things

00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:54.000
That are difficult

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:56.000
So we've talked about, what is judgment?

00:37:56.000 --> 00:37:57.000
How do you understand judgment?

00:37:57.000 --> 00:37:59.000
And you know, hell talk in the Bible

00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:00.000
And you know, all that

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:01.000
So if you missed some of that

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:04.000
You can go back in previous sermons on our podcast

00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:05.000
And catch that

00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:07.000
But at any rate, that's kind of what we've been doing

00:38:07.000 --> 00:38:09.000
So I thought in this message

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:11.000
I wanted to give it a little bit of like

00:38:11.000 --> 00:38:12.000
The kind of catch-all

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:15.000
Because I realize in kind of casting that vision

00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:17.000
There's been certain things I've kind of sidestepped

00:38:17.000 --> 00:38:18.000
Or ignored

00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:21.000
For example, the words antichrist

00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:23.000
I don't think have come from my lips

00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:24.000
Except maybe last week

00:38:24.000 --> 00:38:25.000
Because I was referencing this coming sermon

00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:26.000
You know, so

00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:29.000
You know, the dragon of revelations

00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:31.000
You know, I just haven't gotten into some of that

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:35.000
So I wanted to kind of in this final message

00:38:35.000 --> 00:38:36.000
Kind of do a little bit of a catch-all

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:39.000
And just touch on some topics and things

00:38:39.000 --> 00:38:40.000
Where you're like, but what about that?

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:41.000
Because I realize

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:45.000
Like this is totally a thing in Christian culture

00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:48.000
You know, and I think some of this needs to be addressed

00:38:48.000 --> 00:38:49.000
And kind of thought through

00:38:49.000 --> 00:38:50.000
If you're kind of wondering like

00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:53.000
What's Pastor Brett's thoughts on all that?

00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:54.000
You know, end times prophecies

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:55.000
And you know, things like that

00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:58.000
So that's where we're kind of going in this message

00:38:58.000 --> 00:38:59.000
So with that in mind

00:38:59.000 --> 00:39:00.000
The title of my message is

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:04.000
Resisting End Times Speculative Craziness

00:39:04.000 --> 00:39:08.000
And not the most succinct of titles

00:39:08.000 --> 00:39:11.000
But hopefully you get the heart of it

00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:12.000
So what I'm going to do is

00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:13.000
Just kind of walk us through

00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:16.000
Four kind of, I don't know

00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:19.000
Suggestions or four T's

00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:23.000
To avoiding that kind of thing

00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:24.000
And in the process hopefully

00:39:24.000 --> 00:39:26.000
I'll touch on some of the stuff I was alluding to

00:39:26.000 --> 00:39:30.000
So first, to avoid end times theology hot takes

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:36.000
Be attuned to the genre and the context of Scripture

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:38.000
This is very important

00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:40.000
Where in essence we end up taking things

00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:42.000
That are highly poetic and symbolic

00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:44.000
And kind of allegorical in a sense

00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:48.000
And we end up trying to like map it

00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:53.000
Very specifically onto 21st century

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.000
You know, happenings and such

00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:58.000
So we do this a lot with what's known

00:39:58.000 --> 00:40:00.000
As I mentioned, apocalyptic literature

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:03.000
So apocalyptic, you're like, what is that?

00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:05.000
So this is like small portions of the words of Jesus

00:40:05.000 --> 00:40:08.000
Like Mark 13, Matthew 24, Luke 17

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:11.000
As well as the entire book of Revelation

00:40:11.000 --> 00:40:14.000
And so this is when you're thinking of like

00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:17.000
The classic kind of apocalyptic text

00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:20.000
You know, the moon shall turn to blood

00:40:20.000 --> 00:40:24.000
A third of the stars shall fall from the sky

00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:25.000
You know, this kind of language

00:40:25.000 --> 00:40:28.000
And people start to take that all quite literally

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:30.000
Or just get very confused

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:33.000
Or again try to like map it onto a certain event

00:40:33.000 --> 00:40:35.000
If that happens, well then this will trigger

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:37.000
The apocalypse of this or that

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:40.000
And it just becomes a kind of a whole thing

00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:42.000
So what I want to go back to

00:40:42.000 --> 00:40:45.000
Is to kind of ground this a bit

00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:48.000
To talk about apocalyptic literature

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:49.000
Like what is this?

00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:51.000
So this style of writing

00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:53.000
In speaking and communicating

00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:54.000
This was like a genre

00:40:54.000 --> 00:40:56.000
Like it kind of popped up

00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:58.000
In what's known as the intertestamental period

00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:00.000
So you had the 400 years

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:02.000
In between the ending of the Old Testament

00:41:02.000 --> 00:41:03.000
And those writings

00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:05.000
And the beginning of the New

00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:07.000
And this was a time

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:09.000
Where for the people of God

00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:11.000
It was somewhat of a disaster

00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:13.000
Had a few highlights

00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:14.000
Like if you've read some of the history

00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:15.000
Of the Maccabees and such

00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:16.000
Had some moments of like

00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:18.000
Yes, we're liberated and we're free

00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:19.000
As the Jewish people

00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:20.000
And the people of God and all that

00:41:20.000 --> 00:41:21.000
Mostly though it was

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:24.000
Empire after empire after empire

00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:26.000
The Persians and the Greeks

00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:27.000
And then finally the Romans

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:29.000
I mean it was just conquest after conquest

00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:31.000
And so what did this do?

00:41:31.000 --> 00:41:33.000
This starts to get

00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:35.000
There's a cultural vibe

00:41:35.000 --> 00:41:37.000
You've been in a culture with vibes

00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:41.000
Like moods settle upon a people

00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:45.000
And kind of in that

00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:48.000
It's like they started to wrestle with

00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:50.000
Kind of this challenge

00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:52.000
Is this just how history is going to play out?

00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:54.000
The people of God just struggle?

00:41:54.000 --> 00:41:56.000
The people of God just get oppressed?

00:41:56.000 --> 00:42:00.000
And beastly empires just have their day

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:02.000
And God doesn't even care?

00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:03.000
Is that just the story

00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:04.000
And how this is going to go?

00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:05.000
No!

00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:07.000
And that's where apocalyptic literature

00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:10.000
Emerges from that culture

00:42:10.000 --> 00:42:12.000
From that time

00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:15.000
And in essence it was kind of a way

00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:17.000
Of speaking about

00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:20.000
Beast-like empires and such

00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:24.000
Without like naming them specifically

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:28.000
So like for example

00:42:28.000 --> 00:42:29.000
Most scholars believe

00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:31.000
All but maybe the last chapters

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:33.000
Of the book of Revelation

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:36.000
Are almost certainly about the Roman Empire

00:42:36.000 --> 00:42:38.000
That this was a way of talking about Rome

00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:41.000
Without talking about Rome

00:42:41.000 --> 00:42:43.000
So in essence that's an example

00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:46.000
Where we kind of want to read into it

00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:47.000
Like it's about America

00:42:47.000 --> 00:42:50.000
And these little flying things

00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:52.000
With mouths of

00:42:52.000 --> 00:42:53.000
With sharp teeth

00:42:53.000 --> 00:42:55.000
It's like those are helicopters

00:42:55.000 --> 00:42:57.000
John was seeing a vision of hell

00:42:57.000 --> 00:42:59.000
But he didn't have a language of helicopters

00:42:59.000 --> 00:43:01.000
You know we're like whoa

00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:03.000
We're like running with this

00:43:03.000 --> 00:43:05.000
No probably not

00:43:05.000 --> 00:43:07.000
Mostly this was

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:08.000
That's apocalyptic literature

00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:10.000
It's this way of speaking about empire

00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:13.000
And things going on

00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:15.000
Without actually coming out

00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:16.000
And just like saying it

00:43:16.000 --> 00:43:19.000
So it's highly symbolic

00:43:19.000 --> 00:43:21.000
And vague

00:43:21.000 --> 00:43:23.000
But it's vague on purpose

00:43:23.000 --> 00:43:25.000
Which is to say by the way

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:26.000
Not simply that

00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:27.000
So it's just about Rome

00:43:27.000 --> 00:43:29.000
And has no application

00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:30.000
No it's like

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:33.000
I think in most ways it was about Rome

00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:34.000
But it is

00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:35.000
There is application

00:43:35.000 --> 00:43:36.000
There is a kind of bridge

00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:37.000
That can be built

00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:40.000
To other beast-like empires

00:43:40.000 --> 00:43:42.000
How are we the people of God

00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:44.000
In cultures

00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:46.000
And in at times nation states

00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:47.000
Running amok

00:43:47.000 --> 00:43:48.000
Or doing things that are acting

00:43:48.000 --> 00:43:49.000
In ways that aren't in alignment

00:43:49.000 --> 00:43:50.000
With the heart of God

00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:51.000
And how are we to be

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:53.000
So I think there's

00:43:53.000 --> 00:43:54.000
Connections there

00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:55.000
But at the same time

00:43:55.000 --> 00:43:56.000
We get into trouble

00:43:56.000 --> 00:43:58.000
When we start obsessively

00:43:58.000 --> 00:44:01.000
Trying to map everything

00:44:01.000 --> 00:44:03.000
From that chapter

00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:04.000
Or that book

00:44:04.000 --> 00:44:06.000
To the 21st century

00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:07.000
Into our own day and time

00:44:07.000 --> 00:44:08.000
So that leads us

00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:09.000
To the second key

00:44:09.000 --> 00:44:12.000
We must focus on Christ

00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:13.000
And becoming a person

00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:16.000
Of great love

00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:17.000
Not so much on

00:44:17.000 --> 00:44:20.000
In time speculation

00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:21.000
